refore, the sum of 12.34 and 56.78 is 69.12.\n\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Adding numbers with decimals follows the same principle as adding whole numbers, but you need to ensure that the decimal points are aligned. Here's how you can add 12.34 and 56.78 step by step:\n\n1. Align the numbers by their decimal points:\n   ```\n   12.34\n   +56.78\n   ```\n\n2. Add the digits in the hundredths place:\n   ```\n   4 + 8 = 12\n   ```\n   Write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tenths place.\n\n3. Add the digits in the tenths place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n   3 + 7 + 1 = 11\n   ```\n   Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the units place.\n\n4. Add the digits in the units place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n   2 + 6 + 1 = 9\n   ```\n\n5. Add the digits in the tens place:\n   ```\n   1 + 0 = 1\n   ```\n\n6. Now, we have:\n   ```\n   12.34\n   +56.78\n   ------\n   69.12\n   ```\n\nTherefore, the sum of 12.34 and 56.78 is 69.12. <|User|>That makes sense. Can you show me how to add 123.456 and 789.123?\n<think>\nCertainly! Adding numbers with decimals, such as 123.456 and 789.123, follows the same principle as adding whole numbers, but you need to ensure that the decimal points are aligned. Here's how you can add 123.456 and 789.123 step by step:\n\n1. Align the numbers by their decimal points:\n   ```\n   123.456\n   +789.123\n   ```\n\n2. Add the digits in the thousandths place:\n   ```\n   6 + 3 = 9\n   ```\n\n3. Add the digits in the hundredths place:\n   ```\n   5 + 2 = 7\n   ```\n\n4. Add the digits in the tenths place:\n   ```\n   4 + 1 = 5\n   ```\n\n5. Add the digits in the units place:\n   ```\n   3 + 9 = 12\n   ```\n   Write down 2 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\n6. Add the digits in the tens place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n   2 + 8 + 1 = 11\n   ```\n   Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\n7. Add the digits in the hundreds place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n   1 + 7 + 1 = 9\n   ```\n\n8. Add the digits in 