ts place) and moving to the left. Here's the step-by-step calculation:\n\n1. Align the numbers:\n   ```\n     345678\n   + 876543\n   ```\n\n2. Add the digits in the units place:\n   ```\n     8\n   + 3\n   ---\n     11\n   ```\n   Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\n3. Add the digits in the tens place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n     7\n   + 4\n   + 1\n   ---\n     12\n   ```\n   Write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\n4. Add the digits in the hundreds place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n     6\n   + 5\n   + 1\n   ---\n     12\n   ```\n   Write down 2 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\n5. Add the digits in the thousands place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n     5\n   + 6\n   + 7\n   + 1\n   ---\n     19\n   ```\n   Write down 9 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\n6. Add the digits in the ten-thousands place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n     4\n   + 7\n   + 8\n   + 1\n   ---\n     20\n   ```\n   Write down 0 and carry over 2 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\n7. Add the digits in the hundred-thousands place along with the carry-over:\n   ```\n     3\n   + 8\n   + 2\n   ---\n     13\n   ```\n   Write down 3 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\n8. Finally, add the digits in the millions place:\n   ```\n     1\n   + 0\n   ---\n     1\n   ```\n   Write down 1.\n\nSo, the sum of 345678 and 876543 is 1222221.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>The sum of 345678 and 876543 is 1222221. <|User|>I see the pattern now. The sum of 345678 and 876543 is 1222221. Let's do one more: 456789 + 987654.\n<think>\nTo find the sum of 456789 and 987654, we can follow the same process of aligning the numbers by their place values and then adding them digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the units place) and moving to the left. Here's the step-by-step calculation:\n\n1. Align the numbers:\n   ```\n     456789\n   + 987654\n   ```\n\n2. Add the digits in the units place:\n   ```\n     9\n   + 4\n   ---\n 