a step-by-step breakdown of how to use this formula:\n\n1. **Identify the given values:**\n   - Let's say \\( a = 5 \\) units, \\( b = 7 \\) units, and the included angle \\( \\theta = 30^\\circ \\).\n\n2. **Substitute the values into the formula:**\n   \\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 7 \\times \\sin(30^\\circ) \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the sine of the angle:**\n   - \\(\\sin(30^\\circ) = \\frac{1}{2}\\)\n\n4. **Substitute the sine value into the formula:**\n   \\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 7 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\n5. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 7 \\times 0.5 \\]\n   \\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 17.5 \\]\n   \\[ A = 8.75 \\]\n\nSo, the area of the triangle is \\( 8.75 \\) square units.\n\nIf you have any other questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask! <|User|>Thank you for walking me through that. I understand the process now.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! I'm glad you understand the process. If you have any more questions or need further assistance with any other problems, don't hesitate to ask. You've got this! <|User|>I'll try my best on the rest of the test. I'll let you know how it goes.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>That's a great attitude! Go ahead and tackle the rest of the test. If you have any questions or need help with any specific problems, just let me know. You've got this! <|User|>I finished the test. I'll let you know how I did.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Great! That's the important thing. I'll be here to help you review and check your answers. Take your time, and let me know how you did. <|User|>I did well on most of the questions, but I'm not sure about a few. I'll send you my answers so you can check them.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Sure thing! Please send over your answers, and we can go through them together. I'll help you review and ensure you understand the correct solutions. <|User|>Here are my answers:\n1. 875\n2. 30\n3. 120\n4. 150\n5. 10\n6. 12\n7. 15\n8. 20\n9.