Multiply each digit of the bottom number by each digit of the top number**:\n   - Start with the units place of the bottom number (7):\n     ```\n     239478\n   \u00d7    7\n   --------\n     1676346\n     ```\n   - Move to the tens place of the bottom number (3):\n     ```\n     239478\n   \u00d7   30\n   --------\n     718434\n     ```\n   - Move to the hundreds place of the bottom number (9):\n     ```\n     239478\n   \u00d7   900\n   --------\n    2155302\n     ```\n   - Move to the thousands place of the bottom number (7):\n     ```\n     239478\n   \u00d7  7000\n   --------\n  16763460\n     ```\n   - Move to the ten thousands place of the bottom number (2):\n     ```\n     239478\n   \u00d7 20000\n   --------\n  47895600\n     ```\n\n2. **Shift the results to the left**:\n   - The results are already shifted to the left as we move to the left in the bottom number.\n\n3. **Add up all the products**:\n   - Start from the rightmost column and move to the left, adding up all the products:\n     ```\n     239478\n   \u00d7 277937\n   --------\n     1676346\n     7184340\n    21553020\n   478956000\n   478956000\n   478956000\n   478956000\n   ---------\n   650038000\n   ```\n\nSo, the product of 239478 and 277937 is 650038000.\n\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>The standard algorithm for multiplication involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number, and then adding up all the products. Here's a more detailed explanation:\n\n1. **Write the numbers one below the other**: Align the numbers by their place values, with the digits of one number directly below the digits of the other number.\n2. **Multiply each digit of the bottom number by each digit of the top number**: Start from the rightmost digit of the bottom number and move to the left. Multiply each digit of the bottom number by each digit of the top number, writing the results in a grid or in a separate row.\n3. **Shift the results to the left**: For each digit in the bottom number, sh