ard algorithm for addition involves adding the digits column by column from right to left, carrying over any values that exceed 9. Here's how we can solve the problem 677509 + 712851 using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. Start with the units place:\n   ```\n   9 + 1 = 10\n   ```\n   Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\n2. Move to the tens place:\n   ```\n   0 + 5 + 1 (carried over) = 6\n   ```\n   Write down 6.\n\n3. Move to the hundreds place:\n   ```\n   5 + 8 + 1 (carried over) = 14\n   ```\n   Write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\n4. Move to the thousands place:\n   ```\n   7 + 2 + 1 (carried over) = 10\n   ```\n   Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\n5. Move to the ten-thousands place:\n   ```\n   7 + 1 + 1 (carried over) = 9\n   ```\n   Write down 9.\n\n6. Move to the hundred-thousands place:\n   ```\n   6 + 7 = 13\n   ```\n   Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\n7. Finally, move to the hundred-thousands place again:\n   ```\n   1 (carried over)\n   ```\n   Write down 1.\n\nTherefore, the sum of 677509 and 712851 using the standard algorithm is 1390360.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>The sum of 677509 and 712851 using the standard algorithm is 1390360. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>That makes sense. Can you also show me how to solve it using the partial sums method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The partial sums method involves breaking down each number into its place values and then adding those place values separately. Here's how we can solve the problem 677509 + 712851 using the partial sums method:\n\n1. Break down each number into its place values:\n   ```\n   677509 = 600000 + 70000 + 7000 + 500 + 9\n   712851 = 700000 + 10000 + 2000 + 800 + 50 + 1\n   ```\n\n2. Add the place values separately:\n   ```\n   600000 + 70000 + 7000 + 500 + 9 = 677509\n   700000 + 10000 + 2000 + 800 + 50 + 1 = 712851\n   ```\n\n3. Add the partial sums together:\n   ```\n   677509\n   +712851\n   ------\n   1390360\n   ```\n\nTherefore, the sum of 677509 and 712851 using the partial sums method is 1390360.\n<\uff5cAssi