?\n<think>\nCertainly! Let's use the example of adding 1234 and 5678 using the partial sums method. Here's how you can do it:\n1. Break down each whole number into its place values:\n   ```\n   1234 = 1000 + 200 + 30 + 4\n   5678 = 5000 + 600 + 70 + 8\n   ```\n2. Add the thousands place values together:\n   ```\n   1000 + 5000 = 6000\n   ```\n3. Add the hundreds place values together:\n   ```\n   200 + 600 = 800\n   ```\n4. Add the tens place values together:\n   ```\n   30 + 70 = 100\n   ```\n5. Add the units place values together:\n   ```\n   4 + 8 = 12\n   ```\n6. Combine the results from steps 2 to 5:\n   ```\n   6000 + 800 + 100 + 12 = 6912\n   ```\nIn this case, the sum is 6912.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Let's use the example of adding 1234 and 5678 using the partial sums method. Here's how you can do it:\n1. Break down each whole number into its place values:\n   ```\n   1234 = 1000 + 200 + 30 + 4\n   5678 = 5000 + 600 + 70 + 8\n   ```\n2. Add the thousands place values together:\n   ```\n   1000 + 5000 = 6000\n   ```\n3. Add the hundreds place values together:\n   ```\n   200 + 600 = 800\n   ```\n4. Add the tens place values together:\n   ```\n   30 + 70 = 100\n   ```\n5. Add the units place values together:\n   ```\n   4 + 8 = 12\n   ```\n6. Combine the results from steps 2 to 5:\n   ```\n   6000 + 800 + 100 + 12 = 6912\n   ```\nIn this case, the sum is 6912. <|User|>Thank you for the examples. This has been very helpful.\n<think>\nYou're welcome! If you have any more questions or need further assistance with math problems, feel free to ask. I'm here to help.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! If you have any more questions or need further assistance with math problems, feel free to ask. I'm here to help. <|User|>Could you provide an example of using the standard algorithm for adding decimals?\n<think>\nCertainly! Let's use the example of adding 12.345 and 5.678 using the standard algorithm. Here's how you can do it:\n1. Align the numbers by t